Hi Thorsten,

On Mon, Feb 01, 2021 at 05:10:08PM +0000, Thorsten Alteholz wrote:
> 
> I don't see that the license is "AGPL or OSL" and according to
>  https://wiki.debian.org/DFSGLicenses#Open_Software_License_.28OSL.29_v1.1
> the OSL is not compatible with DFSG.
> 
> But I just had a short look and you can try to convice me :-).

OK, OSL is just an alternative option for the license.  As the DESCRIPTION
file of the package specifies, the license for the code is

      License: AGPL-3 | file LICENSE

So for Debian we simply provde the code AGPL-3 licensed.  The intention
of the authors becomes clear when reading the file NEWS:

    dual licensing the package with AGPLv3 and OSL based on user request

I hope this clarifies the license situation and re-uploaded to new.

Kind regards

        Andreas.

